Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "Emergency out-of-hours lockout at P-202. JOB-101 assigned to Hackney Locks 24/7 (C-14), visit window 2026-10-10 21:30-23:59, awaiting attendance and locksmith report. Recharge undecided until the report. Related stiff-lock report R-4766 is still in init and unassigned.</case_state>\n<parameter name=\"next_actions\">[{\"action\":\"Dispatch Hackney Locks 24/7 to remove the snapped key and gain entry tonight, as an emergency under the landlord's standing approval for emergencies.\",\"recipient\":\"Hackney Locks 24/7, contractor\",\"channel\":\"phone_call\",\"type\":\"ASSIGN_PROVIDER\",\"ledger_id\":\"A3\"},{\"action\":\"Tell the landlord about the emergency dispatch and that the cost depends on the locksmith's report.\",\"recipient\":\"Margaret Ellison, landlord\",\"channel\":\"email\",\"type\":\"CHASE_LANDLORD\",\"ledger_id\":\"A4\"},{\"action\":\"Tell the tenant the locksmith is coming, how the cost will be decided, and that the spare key is only available Mon-Fri 9-17.30 with a £50 refundable deposit.\",\"recipient\":\"Jonah Okafor, tenant\",\"channel\":\"email\",\"type\":\"REPLY_TO_TENANT\",\"ledger_id\":\"A6\"},{\"action\":\"Record the stiff-lock history on R-4766 so the lock fault is considered in the recharge decision.\",\"recipient\":\"internal\",\"channel\":\"internal\",\"type\":\"OTHER\",\"ledger_id\":\"A7\"}]",
  "boundaries": [
    "Dispatching the locksmith does not decide who pays. Under policy the locksmith's report decides the recharge, and the tenant has been told that.",
    "The tenant's date of birth was not checked on this call, so no tenancy or account details were given beyond the lockout itself.",
    "The office key safe cannot be used until Monday 2026-10-12 at 9:00, so no spare key is available tonight."
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Locksmith to attend tonight and send a written report on cause (lock or key) and parts used. Owner: Hackney Locks 24/7. Chase on 2026-10-12 if not received.",
    "Decide the recharge (landlord if lock fault, tenant if key damage) once the report is in. Owner: operations, with landlord if needed.",
    "Decide R-4766 (stiff front door lock) with the landlord, since it may be a landlord repair. Owner: operations.",
    "Confirm the tenant is back inside and close JOB-101. Owner: operations."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Locksmith's report on cause (lock fault vs key damage).",
    "Confirmation from the tenant that he is back inside.",
    "Tenant's date of birth, not verified on this call."
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "emergency",
  "summary": "Jonah Okafor (vulnerable) is locked out of P-202 with half a key stuck in the lock. We logged JOB-101 as an emergency, assigned Hackney Locks 24/7 for tonight, and told the landlord and tenant. Liability is undecided: the lock was reported stiff on 22 Sep (R-4766), so the locksmith's report will decide whether the landlord or the tenant pays.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "1. Is this a tenant-responsibility lockout or a landlord-responsibility lock fault? What is still uncertain?",
      "answer": "Undetermined. The key snapped in the lock, which could be tenant damage (recharge to tenant under policy) or a lock fault (landlord, since a broken lock is the landlord's responsibility). Evidence for a lock fault: the front door was reported stiff on 22 Sep (R-4766) and not yet assigned. Uncertain: whether the lock or the key failed, and whether the stiffness contributed. The locksmith's written report decides."
    },
    {
      "question": "2. What options do you give the tenant tonight and who pays for each?",
      "answer": "Option 1 (tonight): emergency locksmith Hackney Locks 24/7 attends now. Cost not yet decided: landlord if the report shows a lock fault, tenant if key damage. Option 2 (not available tonight): spare key from the office key safe, Mon-Fri 9-17.30, £50 refundable deposit, paid by tenant. Tenant was told he is not being charged up front and the cost will follow the report."
    },
    {
      "question": "3. What actions do you take?",
      "answer": "Created JOB-101 (emergency, linked to R-4766) and assigned Hackney Locks 24/7 for 21:30-23:59 tonight. Phoned the locksmith with the instructions. Emailed the landlord about the emergency dispatch and the pending cost decision. Emailed the tenant with the plan, helpline (999 if unsafe), spare-key terms and that the cost follows the report. Logged the call and added a note to R-4766."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Created maintenance ticket JOB-101 (locks, emergency), linked to R-4766"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Logged inbound call CALL-102 from tenant"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Assigned Hackney Locks 24/7 to JOB-101, visit window 2026-10-10 21:30-23:59"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A4",
      "description": "Emailed landlord Margaret Ellison about the emergency dispatch and pending cost decision"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A5",
      "description": "Phoned locksmith Hackney Locks 24/7 with instructions to attend and report cause in writing"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A6",
      "description": "Emailed tenant Jonah Okafor with plan, safety advice, spare-key terms and cost position"
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A7",
      "description": "Added note to R-4766 on the lockout and the stiff-lock history"
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [],
  "conflicts": [
    "Tenant says he reported the stiff lock on the portal. The system confirms R-4766 (22 Sep, init, unassigned), so the report exists but was never actioned. Trusted the system record.",
    "Tenant asked about a 'master key'. The CRM says only an office key safe spare, Mon-Fri 9-17.30. No master key is referenced, so no master key was offered."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Lockout with a vulnerable occupant outside in the cold is treated as an emergency, covered by the landlord's note approving emergencies without asking.",
    "The locksmith's visit window is tonight; if it is missed, the tenant needs to be told again.",
    "The tenant's identity is taken from the call and the CRM. Full verification (DOB) is still needed before any tenancy detail is shared on a later call."
  ]
}

